{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>On that day</b> — This verse too is a sign that the prophecy concerns the future. <i>And a fountain shall be opened</i> — in its plain sense. Rabbi Moses the Kohen said: it is a metaphor, like <i>and I will sprinkle pure water upon you and you shall be cleansed</i>; therefore after it, <i>the spirit of impurity</i> is reversed into the holy spirit."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:56.756147383Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}